{
  "summary": "Exposes decoded redeem scripts and witness scripts in transaction inputs across RPC and REST endpoints (`getrawtransaction` verbosity 2, `getblock` verbosity 2 and 3, and `/rest/block/`). When previous output undo data is available, it identifies P2SH, P2WSH, and nested SegWit inputs and populates optional `redeemScript` and `witnessScript` objects containing disassembly (`asm`), descriptors (`desc`), script type (`type`), and address. Extraction logic is implemented in `GetRedeemAndWitnessScripts` within the script solver module.",
  "problem": "Callers inspecting spent inputs in block and transaction RPCs cannot view executed redeem or witness scripts without manually parsing pushdata out of the `scriptSig` or `txinwitness` stack and passing it to `decodescript`.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description cites motivation from long-standing issue #27391 and prior attempt #8849."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "Added release notes and applied a minor refactor in `core_io.cpp` reusing an existing loop variable.",
  "card": "Adds decoded redeemScript and witnessScript objects to transaction inputs in getrawtransaction (verbosity 2), getblock (verbosity 2 and 3), and the REST block endpoints when block undo data is available. Currently, block explorers and auditors examining P2SH, P2WSH, or nested SegWit spends must manually parse pushdata from scriptSig or witness stacks and run external decodescript calls. The change implements GetRedeemAndWitnessScripts in the solver module to extract and format script disassembly, descriptors, script types, and addresses, addressing feature request #27391.",
